# Option 1 - Single Pod Processing (ShedLock)

## a. Scheduler Execution

1.⁠ ⁠All application pods start.
2.⁠ ⁠ShedLock ensures only one pod acquires the scheduler lock.
3.⁠ ⁠Remaining pods exit without processing.
4.⁠ ⁠The selected pod starts batch execution.

---

## b. Batch Claim

1.⁠ ⁠Atomically claim 100 Pending (⁠ STA201 ⁠) notifications.
2.⁠ ⁠Commit the transaction.
3.⁠ ⁠Continue only if records are returned.

---

## c. Notification Processing

1.⁠ ⁠Create 5 worker threads using ExecutorService / Virtual Threads.
2.⁠ ⁠Process all claimed notifications concurrently.
3.⁠ ⁠Perform email retries based on business configuration.

---

## d. Status Update

1.⁠ ⁠Email Success → Update notification to ⁠ STA203 (Completed) ⁠.
2.⁠ ⁠Email Failure → Update notification based on current business rule.

---

## e. Continue Processing

1.⁠ ⁠Atomically claim the next batch of 100 records.
2.⁠ ⁠Repeat until no Pending notifications remain.
3.⁠ ⁠Scheduler exits.

---

## Advantages

•⁠  ⁠Simple implementation.
•⁠  ⁠No duplicate processing.
•⁠  ⁠No race conditions.
•⁠  ⁠No distributed coordination.
•⁠  ⁠Lowest implementation risk.

---

## Disadvantages

•⁠  ⁠Only one pod participates.
•⁠  ⁠Throughput limited to a single JVM.

